{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b9a71992-df45-44dc-8ae7-d7dc6722dc1d",
    "name": "DropCore API - Phase 1",
    "description": "# DropCore Phase 1\n\nTests the Create a Hold contract against a local DropCore instance.\n\n## Before running\n\n1. Start PostgreSQL with `docker compose up -d`.\n2. Start DropCore with `mvn spring-boot:run`.\n3. Load `dev/seed.sql` if the demo event is not present.\n4. Select the **DropCore Local** environment.\n\n## Recommended workflow\n\nRun the requests in order, or run the entire collection. **1 - Create a new hold** generates a fresh customer UUID and idempotency keys for each run. The following requests reuse those values to verify successful replay and the one-active-reservation rule.\n\nNo request body is sent because Phase 1 always requests exactly one ticket.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Service health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/actuator/health",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "actuator",
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Checks that the Spring Boot application is running and can reach its configured dependencies. Expected response: `200 OK` with status `UP`."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Health endpoint returns 200', function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('Application reports UP', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('UP');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Create a hold workflow",
      "description": "Run these requests in order. The first request initializes fresh run-specific values; the replay and conflict requests deliberately reuse them.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1 - Create a new hold",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// A fresh customer makes this request repeatable across collection runs.",
                  "const runId = Date.now().toString();",
                  "pm.environment.set('customerId', pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));",
                  "pm.environment.set('idempotencyKey', `postman-hold-${runId}`);",
                  "pm.environment.set('alternativeIdempotencyKey', `postman-hold-${runId}-other`);",
                  "pm.environment.unset('reservationId');",
                  "pm.environment.unset('originalExpiresAt');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('First request returns 201 Created', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const uuidPattern = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[1-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response is a HELD reservation for the requested event', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.reservationId).to.match(uuidPattern);",
                  "    pm.expect(body.eventId).to.eql(pm.environment.get('eventId'));",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('HELD');",
                  "    pm.expect(Date.parse(body.expiresAt)).to.be.above(Date.now());",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Location identifies the new reservation', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.eql(`/v1/reservations/${body.reservationId}`);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// These values are used to prove that replay returns the original snapshot.",
                  "pm.environment.set('reservationId', body.reservationId);",
                  "pm.environment.set('originalExpiresAt', body.expiresAt);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "{{customerId}}",
                "description": "Local-development identity only. This is not production authentication.",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{idempotencyKey}}",
                "description": "Opaque retry key. Must contain 1 to 128 characters.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates one five-minute ticket hold. There is intentionally no request body in v1. A new successful request returns `201 Created` and stores the reservation ID and expiry for subsequent assertions."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2 - Replay the same hold request",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Successful replay returns 200 OK', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Replay returns the original result snapshot', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.reservationId).to.eql(pm.environment.get('reservationId'));",
                  "    pm.expect(body.eventId).to.eql(pm.environment.get('eventId'));",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('HELD');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.expiresAt).to.eql(pm.environment.get('originalExpiresAt'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "{{customerId}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{idempotencyKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Retries the exact same operation with the same idempotency key. Expected response: `200 OK`, with the same reservation ID and original expiry timestamp as request 1."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3 - Reject a second active hold",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Second key for the same customer returns 409', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Error is ACTIVE_RESERVATION_EXISTS', function () {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.code).to.eql('ACTIVE_RESERVATION_EXISTS');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.message).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "{{customerId}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{alternativeIdempotencyKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Uses a different idempotency key for the customer who already owns a HELD reservation. Expected response: `409 Conflict` with `ACTIVE_RESERVATION_EXISTS`. This finalized business outcome is persisted for replay."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4 - Replay the active-reservation conflict",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Finalized conflict replays as 409', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('ACTIVE_RESERVATION_EXISTS');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "{{customerId}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "{{alternativeIdempotencyKey}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Repeats request 3 to demonstrate that finalized `409` business outcomes are idempotently replayed."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Validation and error cases",
      "description": "Independent negative tests. They use dynamic UUIDs where appropriate and do not depend on the successful workflow.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Missing Idempotency-Key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Missing key returns a JSON 400 error', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('INVALID_REQUEST');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "{{$guid}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Omits the required idempotency header. Expected response: `400 Bad Request` with `INVALID_REQUEST`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Invalid customer UUID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Invalid identity returns a JSON 400 error', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('INVALID_REQUEST');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "not-a-uuid",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "invalid-customer-test",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Supplies a malformed local customer identity. Expected response: `400 Bad Request` with `INVALID_REQUEST`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Idempotency key exceeds 128 characters",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Oversized key returns a JSON 400 error', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('INVALID_REQUEST');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "{{$guid}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
                "description": "Exactly 129 ASCII characters.",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{eventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{eventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Checks the contract's 128-character upper bound. Expected response: `400 Bad Request` with `INVALID_REQUEST`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Event does not exist",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Unknown event returns 404', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('EVENT_NOT_FOUND');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Demo-Customer-Id",
                "value": "{{$guid}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Idempotency-Key",
                "value": "unknown-event-{{$timestamp}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/events/{{unknownEventId}}/reservations",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "events",
                "{{unknownEventId}}",
                "reservations"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Targets a valid UUID that is deliberately absent from the demo data. Expected response: `404 Not Found` with `EVENT_NOT_FOUND`."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'Accept', value: 'application/json' });"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": []
}
